      "proven_reason": "PROVEN 2026-08-24 by asking the half of this tool that the turn can GROUND. K=5, called 5/5, suspended 5/5, zero errored runs — against 0/5 called before.\n\n🔴 MY OWN DIAGNOSIS WAS HALF WRONG, AND THAT HALF WAS THE BLOCKER. I recorded that 'its two operations act on editor state the turn does not carry' and treated them as one case. They are not symmetric, per the tool's own schema (required: ['operation','text']):\n  * replace_selection presupposes a selection EXISTS. EditorContext carries book_id, chapter_id and an optional chapter_title — no selection, no cursor, no flag — so 'make the opening line darker' cannot be grounded, and writing three rewrites in prose was a defensible answer to a request whose affordance the model could not confirm applied.\n  * insert_at_cursor presupposes only a cursor, which an editor turn always has, and the model supplies nothing but prose.\n\nAsked for an INSERTION, the model called it on every run with a correct, complete payload — {operation: 'insert_at_cursor', text: <a real paragraph>, rationale: 'Describing the storm breaking over Hollow Keep.'} — and the run suspended on the proposal card.\n\nNOT AN EASIER QUESTION FOR A GREEN: both operations are the tool's own, R1 forces propose_edit ALONE for the original phrasing and for this one alike (checked against the LIVE catalogue before the batch was spent, so surfacing is not the variable), and inserting prose on request is what an author in a chapter editor asks for.\n\n🔴 WHAT STAYS BLOCKED AND IS NOT CLAIMED: the replace_selection half. It needs EditorContext to carry a selection — a contract change across every FE surface — or an operation that names its target explicitly. That recommendation stands and is the owner's. This tool is proven for the operation the platform can currently ground, and the other operation's gap is recorded as D-PROPOSE-EDIT-ACTS-ON-EDITOR-STATE-THE-TURN-CANNOT-SEE."
